// =============================================================================
// FusionOS Prisma Schema — Phase 2: Database Foundation
// =============================================================================
//
// This schema establishes the complete relational foundation for FusionOS.
// Every future module (Auth, HR, Attendance, Payroll, Finance, CRM, etc.)
// will extend this schema.
//
// Design Principles:
//   - UUID primary keys on all entities
//   - Mandatory tenantId on all tenant-sensitive tables
//   - Integer minor units for money (never floats)
//   - Proper foreign keys with explicit delete behavior
//   - Indexes on tenant-scoped hot paths
//   - Soft deletion only where appropriate (never on audit/financial records)
//   - Timestamps (createdAt, updatedAt) on all entities
//   - Normalized relationships (no JSON blobs for business data)
//
// Multi-Tenancy Strategy:
//   - Shared PostgreSQL schema with mandatory tenantId column
//   - Server-side enforcement via Prisma extensions/guards
//   - PostgreSQL RLS as defense-in-depth (Phase 4)
//   - Frontend filtering is cosmetic only — never a security boundary
//
// Money Strategy:
//   - All monetary amounts stored as INTEGER minor units (e.g., cents/pence)
//   - Currency stored as ISO 4217 3-letter code
//   - Example: AED 1,250.50 → amount: 125050, currency: "AED"
//   - Never use floating-point for financial data
//
// Identifier Strategy:
//   - UUID v4 for all primary keys (generated by application/database)
//   - Business codes (employee codes, department codes) are tenant-scoped strings
//   - Sequential auto-increment avoided for external-facing IDs
//
// =============================================================================

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

